# Grim Hollow Player's Guide 2024: Transformations Hag, Lich, Lycanthrope.
TRANS = {
 "Hag": {
  "intro": "Hags are fey crones who bargain, curse and despoil purity. You become one through a trial, a curse or a deal. Move up a stage when your story earns it, for example by striking a bargain with a powerful Hag or by consuming the flesh of the innocent. You can reverse this Transformation only in Stages 1 and 2, and it takes months or years of work plus a powerful fey who joins a final ritual.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Hag Form and one other Stage 1 Boon of your choice (a Sisterhood). You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Hag Form"], "d": "Hag stage 1: Fey type, natural armor, and one Sisterhood."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon and gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Hag stage 2: Adept of a Sisterhood, plus Iron Sensitivity."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon and gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Hag stage 3: Master of a Sisterhood, plus Purity's Pain."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon and gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Hag stage 4: a capstone Boon, plus Arch-Crone's Hunger."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Hag Form": "You are also a Fey, on top of any other creature types. While you wear no armor, your AC is 13 plus your Dexterity modifier. Pick Strength, Intelligence or Charisma and gain proficiency in saving throws with that ability.",
   "The Green Sisterhood": "Green Hags are deceivers who hoard curses and corrupting magic. You gain Darkvision to 60 feet, or +60 feet if you already have it. You can breathe air and water. You can imitate animal sounds and humanoid voices. A listener can spot the fake with a Study action and a Wisdom (Insight) check against DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier plus your Transformation Stage.",
   "The Red Sisterhood": "Red Hags seem kind but act from selfish motives, and they love a deal that is too good to refuse. You gain Darkvision to 60 feet. You gain proficiency in Deception and Persuasion, or Expertise in any you already have. Your form cannot be changed by any effect. An illusion can hide you only if it makes you Invisible.",
   "The Sea Sisterhood": "Sea Hags thrive on chaos and wear hideous faces. You gain Darkvision to 60 feet. You can breathe air and water and gain a Swim Speed equal to your Speed (or +10 feet if you already have one). As a Magic action, gaze at a creature you can see within 30 feet. It makes a Wisdom save against DC 8 plus your Charisma modifier plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure it takes 1d8 Psychic damage per Transformation Stage.",
   "Adept of the Green Sisterhood": "You gain a Claw attack that deals 1d6 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. You can also cast Invisibility as a Magic action without a spell slot, a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage. You regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Adept of the Red Sisterhood": "You gain a Claw attack that deals 1d6 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. You can also cast Charm Person as a Magic action without a spell slot, with a save DC of 12 plus your Transformation Stage. You can do this a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Adept of the Sea Sisterhood": "You gain a Claw attack that deals 1d6 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. You can also cast Disguise Self as a Magic action without a spell slot, with a save DC of 12 plus your Transformation Stage. You can do this a number of times equal to your Transformation Stage and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Master of the Green Sisterhood": "When you take the Attack action, you can make one extra Claw attack. Your Claw attacks deal an extra 1d6 Poison damage. You also know a dark ritual that makes a Hag Eye or a Gasdra companion. It takes four hours and 200 GP, you choose which one when you take this Boon, and you can have only one such companion at a time. As a Magic action you can regain one expended spell slot by spending Hit Point Dice equal to its level. The slot level can be at most one third of your character level (round up). You can do this once per Long Rest.",
   "Master of the Red Sisterhood": "When you take the Attack action, you can make one extra Claw attack. Your Claw attacks deal an extra 1d4 Psychic damage, and you regain Hit Points equal to that Psychic damage. If a creature under your magical influence (such as Charmed by you) hears you for 1 minute, it makes a Charisma save against DC 14 plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure, it forgets that magic was used on it when your influence ends. You regain this use after a Short or Long Rest. As a Bonus Action, you can spend a Hit Point Die to cast Charm Person.",
   "Master of the Sea Sisterhood": "When you take the Attack action, you can make one extra Claw attack. Your Claw attacks deal an extra 1d6 Slashing damage. As a Bonus Action, show your true face to a Beast or Humanoid within 30 feet that can see it. The target makes a Wisdom save against DC 14 plus your Charisma modifier. On a failure it is Frightened until the start of its next turn. On a success it is immune to this for 24 hours. You regain this use after a Short or Long Rest. As a Magic action, you can spend and roll a Hit Point Die and touch a creature. It can breathe water for a number of minutes equal to the roll.",
   "Evil Eye": "As a Magic action, gaze at a Bloodied Beast or Humanoid within 30 feet that can see your true form. It makes a Wisdom save against DC 14 plus your Charisma modifier. On a failure it drops to 0 Hit Points. On a success it takes 6d8 Psychic damage. You regain this use after a Long Rest.",
   "Grandmother's Curse": "Learn one Shadowsteel curse of your choice. It is always prepared and does not count against your prepared spells. You can cast it once per day without a spell slot or components.",
   "Hideous Appearance (Hag)": "Your body, hair and eyes change into something mortals find abhorrent. Most creatures that see your true form become Hostile and few will trust you, unless the GM says otherwise. You have Disadvantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks. You cannot bear your own reflection. The first time you see it after a Short or Long Rest, make a DC 18 Wisdom save or gain 1 Exhaustion level. Your look follows your Sisterhood. Green: white hair several feet long, and green skin covered in warts and boils. Red: fully red eyes with cat-like pupils, and blood-red skin. Sea: slimy scales, pallid sagging skin, seaweed-like hair and glassy eyes.",
   "Iron Sensitivity": "Iron and steel weapons forged in the mortal realm hurt you. After each Short or Long Rest, the first time one damages you, make a DC 15 Constitution save or be Stunned until the end of your next turn.",
   "Purity's Pain": "Pure things make you physically ill, such as a child hugging a parent, a loyal dog, devout art or a baby's laughter. The GM decides what counts. At the start of each of your turns while you can see the source, you take 3d6 plus your Charisma modifier Psychic damage and cannot use Hag Transformation Boons until the start of your next turn. The first time you take this damage after a Short or Long Rest, make a DC 18 Wisdom save. On a failure you are Frightened while you can see the source.",
   "Arch-Crone's Hunger": "Normal food no longer feeds you. Each day you must eat something strange, cursed or vile, or you gain 1 Exhaustion level that cannot be removed until you feed. If you must eat or drink normal fare, make a DC 18 Constitution save or vomit it up and gain 1 Exhaustion level. Vile foods include the flesh of sapient Humanoids, Fey or Celestials, magical ingredients such as rare herbs or dragon's blood, the pain and suffering of others, and pages of a cursed tome.",
  }
 },
 "Lich": {
  "intro": "A Lich tears its soul from its body and stores it in a soul vessel. This gives great power and costs a slow loss of self. Move up a stage when your story earns it, for example by discovering dark arcane lore or by leading an army of undead. This Transformation cannot be reversed. Only destroying both your body and your soul vessel ends you. Much of your power depends on the soul vessel being charged.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "You gain Undead Form and one other Stage 1 Boon of your choice. You also gain the Stage 1 Flaw, Soul Vessel.", "take": 1, "fixed": ["Undead Form"], "d": "Lich stage 1: Undead type, agelessness, and a soul vessel."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon and gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lich stage 2: undead minions, curses or corrupting spells."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon and gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lich stage 3: stronger spellcasting, undead or healing."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon and gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lich stage 4: a capstone Boon, plus Weight of the Ages."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Undead Form": "You are also an Undead, on top of any other creature types. Turn Undead cannot skip you. You stop aging, cannot be aged by effects, and cannot die of old age. You need no air, food, drink or sleep.",
   "Memori Lichdom": "While your soul vessel is charged, your weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes are magical. Those you make as a Reaction have Advantage. After you deal damage with one, you can use a Bonus Action later that turn and spend a Hit Point Die. Roll it and deal Necrotic damage equal to the result to one target the triggering attack damaged.",
   "Lich Magica": "On your turn, as a Bonus Action, you can spend the charge in your soul vessel for one effect. Regain a spell slot of a level up to your Lich Transformation Stage. Or the next save against your spell before the end of your next turn has Disadvantage. Or the next spell you cast before the end of your next turn deals an extra 1d6 Necrotic damage per Stage to one creature it damaged. Or the next healing spell you cast before the end of your next turn restores an extra 1d6 Hit Points per Stage.",
   "Acolyte of Undeath": "When you drop a Humanoid to 0 Hit Points and it dies, you can use a Reaction to raise it as a Zombie under your control. You can control three at a time. They act on their own Initiative and follow your spoken commands as best they can.",
   "Binding Curse": "As a Bonus Action, choose a creature within 30 feet that can see you. It makes a Charisma save against DC 12 plus your Transformation Stage. On a failure it cannot move more than 30 feet from you for 1 minute, and your weapon attacks and Unarmed Strikes against it deal an extra 2d6 Necrotic damage. You can use this three times and regain all uses after a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Corrupting Magic": "When a spell of yours kills a creature, you can add one effect. You cannot do this to a Construct, an Undead or anything without a soul. Life Force: you regain 1d6 Hit Points per Transformation Stage. Poison: a creature of your choice within 10 feet of the dead one takes 1d6 Poison damage per Stage. Exhaustion: a creature of your choice within 10 feet of the dead one gains 1 Exhaustion level, and a creature can carry only one level from this feature at a time.",
   "Hideous Appearance (Lich)": "Your flesh withers around your bones, your eyes sink and you reek of death. You can suspend this and look like the person you were, but it takes effort and does not last. Your true form shows when you are Bloodied, concentrating on a spell, Unconscious, on hallowed ground, or when you choose. In these cases, or under other extreme stress, the GM can call for a Constitution save and you reveal your form on a failure. The DC is 13 at Stage 2, 16 at Stage 3 and 20 at Stage 4. Non-evil creatures that see your true form become Hostile, unless the GM says otherwise.",
   "Eldritch Concentration": "When you cast a Concentration spell while already concentrating on one, you can spend the charge of your soul vessel to keep the first spell. You gain 1 Exhaustion level. If you cast a third Concentration spell in this time, or lose Concentration any other way, you lose both spells. You regain this use after a Short or Long Rest.",
   "Master of Undeath": "Undead you control through a Lich Boon have Advantage on attack rolls while within 5 feet of you. When such an Undead drops to 0 Hit Points, you can spend the charge of your soul vessel as a Reaction. It then has 1 Hit Point instead, moves up to its Speed and makes an Attack action with Advantage. This does nothing if Radiant damage dropped it to 0.",
   "Unholy Healing": "While your soul vessel is charged, use a Magic action to draw healing from it. At the start of each of your turns for 1 minute, you regain 10 Hit Points, and the vessel keeps its charge. You can do this three times and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Necromantic Dystrophia": "While your soul vessel is not charged, you cannot take the Dash, Dodge or Disengage actions, you cannot take Reactions, and you have Disadvantage on Constitution saves. You also cannot hide your Hideous Appearance (Lich). Charging the vessel with a fitting soul ends these effects.",
   "Eldritch Omniscience": "The number of spells you can learn and prepare rises by 4. After each Short or Long Rest you gain one extra spell slot of a level you choose. When one of your spells kills a creature, you can pull its soul into your soul vessel at once, with no action or Reaction.",
   "Soul-Shattering Attack": "After you make a weapon attack or Unarmed Strike, you can spend the charge in your soul vessel to add the stored soul's Challenge Rating to that attack roll and its damage. If the target dies from it, you can recharge the vessel at once with the soul you just spent. You can use this a number of times equal to 4 plus your Proficiency Bonus and regain all uses after a Long Rest.",
   "Lord of Undeath": "When you use Acolyte of Undeath, you can raise the target as a Ghoul instead of a Zombie.",
   "Soul Vessel": "You tore your soul out and sealed it in a trinket or item no larger than 1 cubic foot, your soul vessel. It has AC 18, Hit Points equal to 10 times your character level and Speed 0. It is immune to Poison, Psychic, and nonmagical Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. It resists Cold, Fire, Lightning, Necrotic, Thunder, and magical Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. While it holds a soul, it is charged. That soul must come from a creature with a Challenge Rating of at least half your character level, and the vessel holds one soul at a time. You can add a soul 2 times per Transformation Stage and regain this after a Long Rest. To capture a soul, hold the vessel and use a Magic action within 1 minute of the creature's death, or a Reaction to its death. The body must be within 60 feet of the vessel. The creature cannot be revived while its soul is stored. If the vessel drops to 0 Hit Points, you must make a new one, which takes a Long Rest. Until then you lose its benefits and have Disadvantage on the first D20 Test after each Short or Long Rest. If you die while your charged vessel is on your plane, its charge is spent and you return as if by Resurrection within 5 feet of it after 1 day. If it is not charged, you return after 7 days.",
   "Weight of the Ages": "Time wears at your form and only your soul vessel holds it together. If the vessel drops to 0 Hit Points, your soul is lost, you die at once and your body crumbles to dust.",
  }
 },
 "Lycanthrope": {
  "intro": "A lycanthrope fights a constant battle between beast and person. You gain the curse by a bite, by the druidic Lunar Sacrament or by another curse or relic. From Stage 1 on, ordinary magic like Remove Curse cannot cure it, and only a Wish-level effect removes it. Move up a stage when your story earns it, for example by killing a mighty foe in hybrid form under a full moon. You choose one Boon per stage, and your hybrid form lasts 1 hour per Transformation Stage.",
  "stages": {
   1: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 1 Boon (your hybrid form) and gain the Stage 1 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lycanthrope stage 1: pick a wolf, bear or rat hybrid form."},
   2: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 2 Boon and gain the Stage 2 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lycanthrope stage 2: a hunting, defense or animal form Boon."},
   3: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 3 Boon and gain the Stage 3 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lycanthrope stage 3: more Hit Points or more savagery."},
   4: {"rule": "Choose one Stage 4 Boon and gain the Stage 4 Flaw.", "take": 1, "fixed": [], "d": "Lycanthrope stage 4: control in hybrid form or deadlier strikes."},
  },
  "opt": {
   "Hybrid Wolf Form": "You are also a Monstrosity. As a Magic action, you turn into a half-wolf hybrid. In this form your Strength becomes 18 unless higher, your Speed rises by 10 feet and you can Dash as a Bonus Action. You cannot cast spells or concentrate on them, and you speak only in short, guttural words. You can use weapons and gear normally. You gain a Claw or Bite that can replace any weapon attack and deals 1d8 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. After the Attack action, you can use a Bonus Action later that turn to attack once with Claw or Bite. The form lasts 1 hour per Transformation Stage. If you chose to enter it, you can leave it with a Magic action on your turn. Flaws may override this.",
   "Hybrid Bear Form": "You are also a Monstrosity. As a Magic action, you turn into a half-bear hybrid. In this form your Strength becomes 20 unless higher and you gain a Climb Speed equal to your Speed. You cannot cast spells or concentrate on them, and you speak only in short, guttural words. You can use weapons and gear normally. You gain a Claw that can replace any weapon attack and deals 1d8 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. After hitting with a Claw, you can use a Bonus Action to grab the target if it is at most one size larger than you. It has the Grappled condition, and the escape DC is 8 plus your Strength modifier plus your Proficiency Bonus. The form lasts 1 hour per Transformation Stage. If you chose to enter it, you can leave it with a Magic action on your turn. Flaws may override this.",
   "Hybrid Rat Form": "You are also a Monstrosity. As a Magic action, you turn into a half-rat hybrid. In this form your Dexterity becomes 18 unless higher and you can Hide or Disengage as a Bonus Action. You gain proficiency in Stealth and can double your Proficiency Bonus on Dexterity (Stealth) checks. You cannot cast spells or concentrate on them, and you speak only in short, guttural words. You can use weapons and gear normally. You gain a Claw or Bite that can replace any weapon attack and deals 1d6 Slashing damage plus your Strength or Dexterity modifier. You are proficient with it and use the same modifier for attack and damage. It is not an Unarmed Strike and cannot replace one. After the Attack action, you can use a Bonus Action later that turn to attack once with Claw or Bite. You have Advantage on Claw or Bite attacks against a target within 5 feet of one of its enemies. The form lasts 1 hour per Transformation Stage. If you chose to enter it, you can leave it with a Magic action on your turn. Flaws may override this.",
   "Lust for the Hunt": "Your curse sometimes takes control. The first time you become Bloodied after a Short or Long Rest, make a DC 10 Wisdom save. Under a full moon you fail automatically. On a failure you enter hybrid form at once and these rules apply until you can end it. You go feral and cannot use your equipment or class features. On your turn you must move toward the nearest creature you can see, smell or hear, favoring Bloodied ones. If you end your move with no creature within 5 feet, you must Dash toward the nearest. If a creature is within 5 feet and you have not used your action, you must make an Attack action with your Claw. When you damage a creature that does not drop to 0, you must keep attacking it that turn. If you start your turn at full Hit Points, you can make a DC 10 Wisdom save to return to normal form on a success. You also return to normal if Remove Curse is cast on you or after 1 hour.",
   "Hunter's Focus": "While in hybrid form, you can use a Bonus Action to mark a creature within 60 feet as your prey. The mark lasts 1 hour or until it dies, and you can mark only one creature at a time. Your melee hits against it deal an extra 1d6 damage of the attack's type. You have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception or Survival) checks to find it.",
   "Iron Pelt": "While in hybrid form, you resist Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage. Magical and silvered weapons ignore this Resistance.",
   "Kindred Form": "You can turn into the animal your curse matches, using that creature's stat block and the rules of Polymorph. Werebear uses Black Bear, wererat uses Giant Rat and werewolf uses Wolf. You look like any other creature of that kind and can talk with them. You cannot speak but you understand languages you know. All gear you wear and carry falls off when you change.",
   "Silver Sensitivity": "In every form you are Vulnerable to Bludgeoning, Piercing and Slashing damage from silvered weapons, and you cannot have Resistance to damage from silvered weapons.",
   "Bestial Vigor": "Your Hit Point maximum rises by your character level and by 1 more each time you gain a level. In hybrid form, you gain 5 Temporary Hit Points at the start of each of your turns.",
   "Shapeshifter's Savagery": "While in hybrid form, your Claw and Bite attacks deal an extra 1d8 Slashing damage, and you are immune to the Charmed and Frightened conditions.",
   "Frayed Thoughts": "Two minds share your head and old memories fade behind midnight hunts. You have Disadvantage on Intelligence checks and saving throws.",
   "Hybrid Form Affinity": "While you are in hybrid form by choice, you speak normally. You can cast spells without Verbal or Somatic components, and without Material components that have no listed GP value. Allies within 20 feet of you have Advantage on Wisdom checks and saving throws.",
   "Savage Instincts": "While in hybrid form, your Claw or Bite deals an extra 1d8 Slashing damage when it hits a Bloodied creature.",
   "Ultimate Predator": "The beast has more control than you do and will break free. If you can see, hear or smell a Bloodied creature, you have Disadvantage on Wisdom saves. At the start of your turn, if you can see, hear or smell an Unconscious creature, make a DC 15 Wisdom save. On a failure you change to hybrid form, or go feral as in Lust for the Hunt if already in it. On a success you are immune to this until a Long Rest. When you kill a creature in hybrid form, you cannot return to normal form until dawn the next day.",
  }
 },
}
